Run records of codegen/c/floatconv_test.go's tests that build a program with clang flags
of their own and run it, written by tackc's porttest/rungen and completed
by tools/corpus --update; see tools/corpus/runs.tck for the format.
-- float-examples-are-sanitizer-clean-1/record --
replaces codegen/c/floatconv_test.go TestFloatExamplesAreSanitizerClean/floats-O0
replaces codegen/c/floatconv_test.go TestFloatExamplesAreSanitizerClean/floats-O2
strict-libs the test compiles its build's C with -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fstrict-flex-arrays=3 at its level and flags itself, which the driver's -w turns off; the runner compiles it so
dir examples/floats
opt 0 2
cflags -fstrict-flex-arrays=3 -fsanitize=address,undefined,float-cast-overflow -fsanitize-address-use-after-return=always -fno-sanitize-recover=all -D_DEFAULT_SOURCE -fno-sanitize-address-globals-dead-stripping -ffinite-loops -mllvm -indvars-predicate-loops=true
lacks stdout "FAIL"
stdout-file examples/floats/output
exit 0
stderr ""
